      <h2>Entrée Efficiency: Chicken Strips vs. Original Cheeseburger</h2>
      <p>When selecting your $7 Meal Deal protein, you face a binary choice: the 3-Piece Chicken Strip Basket or the Original Cheeseburger. Our nutritional and cost audit reveals a decisive winner:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Select the 3-Piece Chicken Strips:</strong> À la carte, the 3pc strips retail for $4.99 and deliver 36 grams of pure whole-muscle breast protein. The chicken strips yield a higher raw wholesale cost for the franchisee, maximizing your consumer arbitrage.</li>
        <li><strong>Avoid the Original Cheeseburger inside the $7 Deal:</strong> The <a href="/items/original-cheeseburger">Original Cheeseburger</a> retails à la carte for roughly $3.29. Ordering it inside the $7 bundle reduces your total net discount from $5.86 down to $4.16. If you crave a burger, save the meal deal for tenders and buy the burger via the 2-for-$5 menu instead.</li>
      </ul>

